---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { GA_MEASUREMENT_ID } from '../../../lib/analytics';

const analyticsAttivo = Boolean(GA_MEASUREMENT_ID);
---

<Layout title="Privacy and cookies" description="How the SanVitoRomano Lovers site handles visitors' data and which cookies it uses.">
  <h1>Privacy and cookies</h1>
  <p class="meta">What data this site collects, why, and how you can decide.</p>

  <h2>Who runs the site</h2>
  <p>
    The site is run by the SanVitoRomano Lovers community. For any question about your data you can
    write to <a href="mailto:info@sanvitoromanolovers.org">info@sanvitoromanolovers.org</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <p>
    The site requires no registration and, for ordinary browsing, does not collect names, email
    addresses or other personal data. The only exception is the photo contest entry form, described
    below. We do not use advertising or profiling cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Photo contest form</h2>
  <p>
    The photo contest page has a form for submitting your photos. Filling it in is optional: data is
    collected only if you choose to take part and press the submit button.
  </p>
  <p>
    The form asks for your <strong>full name</strong>, <strong>email address</strong>,
    <strong>photo title</strong> and the <strong>photo</strong> itself. We use this data only to
    manage your entry in the contest and to send you emails about it. We do not pass it on to third
    parties and do not use it for advertising or newsletters.
  </p>
  <p>
    The form is provided by Tally, an external service embedded in the page: the data you submit is
    collected and stored by Tally on our behalf. For details see
    <a href="https://tally.so/help/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tally's
    privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    After you submit, the name you entered is saved temporarily in your browser for the sole purpose
    of showing it on the thank-you page: it is not sent to our servers and is deleted when you close
    the tab.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can ask at any time to see, correct or delete the data and photos you have submitted by
    writing to <a href="mailto:info@sanvitoromanolovers.org">info@sanvitoromanolovers.org</a>.
  </p>

  {
    analyticsAttivo ? (
      <>
        <h2>Visit statistics (Google Analytics 4)</h2>
        <p>
          To understand how many people visit the site and which pages are read we use Google Analytics
          4, a Google service. Analytics is switched on <strong>only if you accept</strong> in the
          banner shown on your first visit: until you accept, or if you reject, it is not loaded and
          sets no cookies.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you accept, Analytics sets a few cookies in your browser (with names starting with
          <code>_ga</code>, lasting up to two years) and collects aggregated data such as the pages
          visited, the type of device and browser, the language, the approximate geographical area and
          the referring site. The data is processed by Google, which may also store it on servers
          outside the European Union. For details see
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's
          privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How to change your mind</h2>
        <p>
          You can change your choice at any time with the "Cookie preferences" link at the bottom of
          every page. If you reject after accepting, the Analytics cookies are deleted from your
          browser. Your choice is stored only in your browser, not on our servers.
        </p>
      </>
    ) : (
      <>
        <h2>Cookies and statistics</h2>
        <p>At present the site uses no tracking cookies and no visit statistics tools.</p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    The site contains links to external sites (for example Facebook, Instagram, TikTok, WhatsApp,
    OpenStreetMap and the sources of the news). When you follow them, those sites' privacy rules
    apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) you can ask for information about
    the data concerning you, object to its processing and contact the
    <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Italian Data Protection
    Authority</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
